Now I''d like to write about the cons:
There were no blankets in the room, for me it is a big downside, both the reception and the guest manager, and through the guide from the tour operator, were approached, promised today now and never delivered.
The minibar is not replenished, there were 3 sodas and 1 bottle of water at the time of entry, water was not brought at the time of cleaning, had to be carried from the restaurant. No accessories by type: bathrobe, toothbrush,paste,napkins.
There are many "bangleless" facilities on the property, the same as hotel guests. Very many residents since one territory with a hotel. The downside is that, large pool areas, a water park, the beach shares with them, and even a bus. It would be better if the grounds were shared at least on the beach, and there was a separate transfer for residents and guests of the hotel. Very uncomfortable, there''s a crowd of residents on the buses and there''s no room for guests.
The beach isn''t like the picture. It''s not closed to other people, the beach comes from other hotels, occupy sunbeds and it''s not controlled in any way. The "rescuers" as it were, but they don''t even look, saw them twice in the entire stay. The entrance to the sea is not cleaned of debris, the water is dirty when entering, you need to go through the garbage and somewhere deep swimming, which is not convenient for people with children.
All restaurants are closed at night, if you''ve been somewhere on a tour, in the city, on the beach to meet the dawn and didn''t make it to dinner unfortunately you won''t be able to eat anywhere.
Ice cream was only served in the restaurant at lunch, and at dinner the next day. I wish it was freely available in the territory at least at a certain time.
The animation is a little weak, and only takes place by the very first pool.', 3, 'Jul 21', null),
  ('55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555502', 'https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g1069655-d33144231-r1068977972-Azura_World_Hotel-Turkler_Alanya_Turkish_Mediterranean_Coast.html', 'We just enjoyed a week stay in Azura world hotel as a couple from the UK and we had a lovely time :)
The hotel grounds in itself were stunning! The grounds were very well kept and clean and very aesthetically pleasing. The staff around are lovely and are happy to help if you need. We met a lovely waiter who was coming around the pool delivering drinks and taking orders and he was such a lovely man, didn’t get his name but he was around most days!
As it is quite a big hotel you’d expect it to be very busy, but we always managed to get a sunbed, usually in the same spot and it didn’t feel crowded or loud it was very relaxing especially as a couple we were worried that it would be noisy with children but it was absolutely fine.
One recommendation is that there is a large lazy river type look throughout the pools which aren’t actually accessible and just for decoration but I think making it actually into a lazy river would be a very good benefit to the hotel.
The food was okay, the breakfast and lunch were very samey and could have been mixed up and a bit of better quality but nonetheless we always had full plates but could have been more variety for a 5 star- the pancakes and baklava were the best!
We did have a meal at the à la carte restaurant with our stay which was a nice mix up.
The room was very spacious and modern no complaints there!
The hotel beach was gorgeous! Very picturesque and good that there was an hourly shuttle that can take you there and back if you don’t fancy the walk although we did walk back one days after a bit of shopping and only took about 15 minutes if you want to.
Overall I would definitely return to Azura world I had a lovely time, don’t get put off by a few bad reviews as we were worried over a few reviews we had seen but we had the best time!', 4, 'Jul 18', null),
  ('55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555502', 'https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g1069655-d33144231-r1068957328-Azura_World_Hotel-Turkler_Alanya_Turkish_Mediterranean_Coast.html', 'We’ve just returned from a family holiday at Azura World Hotel, and overall our stay was mixed.

The biggest positives were definitely the staff, who were friendly, welcoming, and always happy to help. The hotel was also very clean throughout our stay, and the pools were well maintained and a great place for the family to relax.

On the downside, the hotel itself is quite small and is surrounded by residential areas. We found that many of the local residents weren’t particularly welcoming, which affected the overall atmosphere. The food was decent enough, but the selection became quite repetitive after a few days, so it lacked variety for a longer stay.

Unfortunately, there isn’t much to do within walking distance of the hotel, and the location isn’t ideal if you’re looking to explore the area or enjoy local entertainment. A shuttle service to nearby towns, beaches, or attractions would have made a big difference and improved the overall experience.

Overall, the hotel has some strong points, particularly the excellent staff, cleanliness, and pool facilities. However, the limited location, repetitive food, and lack of things to do nearby mean it’s probably not somewhere we would choose to return to for another family holiday.', 3, 'Jul 18', null),
  ('55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555502', 'https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g1069655-d33144231-r1068910322-Azura_World_Hotel-Turkler_Alanya_Turkish_Mediterranean_Coast.html', 'Rooms are brilliant the atmosphere is very nice good workers more activities to do however food wise is a little issue but i believe they will improve with it but for now everything is very good!', 4, 'Jul 18', null),
  ('55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555502', 'https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g1069655-d33144231-r1068440567-Azura_World_Hotel-Turkler_Alanya_Turkish_Mediterranean_Coast.html', 'First time at this hotel.We chose this hotel after seen impressive photos ..All looks amazing everything its clean,spotless.Modern and new furniture''s everywhere very comfy. All staff professional and very helpful from hospitality to housekeeping.
Looking at photos you think its a big hotel ,actually it''s a medium to small i can say.What you see in presentation include as well residential area- hotel it''s just a central building from what you see in photos.Nobody tells you about this. I was stopped to go in some areas being told -you can''t get acces this is for residents..
The only thing wich is dissapointing its the food .Very basic for a 5* hotel,
Definitely not good value for money what you have to pay for a holiday at Azura World..Its all inclusive and for a top range hotel how its considered having 1 buffet restaurant 1 a''la carte and 1 snack wich offer 5-6 food plates in menu but same low quality.
You can have last meal by 9pm ,not considering the soup what is offered by 11pm as a meal..
Totally dissapointing for a 5* hotel ,keep saying just because everything else it''s at best level.
It''s more then 12 years I come to Antalya and its first time when I get this discrepancies and no good value for money.', 3, 'Jul 15', null),
  ('55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555502', 'https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g1069655-d33144231-r1068210019-Azura_World_Hotel-Turkler_Alanya_Turkish_Mediterranean_Coast.html', 'Regrettably, a holiday in this hotel left an extremely unpleasant draught. I''ll start in order.

1. Check-in and attempted deception.
On the first day they tried to “relocate” us to a lower category hotel Azura Deluxe. We were told that these were the “best terms”, first offered to pay extra, and when we saw our doubts, pretended that they were a “gift”. We refused. Starting a vacation with an attempt at a trivial divorce is extremely unpleasant.

2. Cleaning and tidying.
The room looks chic, you can see there''s a lot of money invested in the design. But it''s disgusting to clean it up. Tables were sticky, dust everywhere, and on the bedside table there was a ball of other people''s hair! How could you not see that? It''s just sloppy.

3. Sea and beach.
The beach is beautifully equipped, the deckchairs are good, but the service is limp. The area of the beach is dirty - there are cigarette butts, bottles and bulls, no one cleans them up. The water''s muddy with debris. And the worst part is the transfer: they take an old, broken bus that arrives already packed with people. For a hotel at this level, it''s a shame.

4. THEFT AND STAFF INDIFFERENCE (MOST IMPORTANTLY!)
It''s overstepped all the mark. The day before he left the room, new $150 sneakers that were in the factory box and bag went missing. Once you hold this bag, you can''t confuse it with garbage -- there were clearly shoes.

We told the receptionist right away. The girl assured me the matter would be resolved in the morning. The next morning, it turned out no one knew anything. We went to the manager. She promised to look at the cameras and resolve the matter before we leave (1:20 p.m. departure). But instead of looking, they just said, “There was no theft of the cleaning lady on the cameras.” The result is that things are gone and we have received no apology or compensation. We are not scandalous and very patient people, but not even apologizing is the height of disrespect.', 1, 'Jul 14', null),
  ('55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555502', 'https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g1069655-d33144231-r1067914037-Azura_World_Hotel-Turkler_Alanya_Turkish_Mediterranean_Coast.html', 'The hotel grounds are beautiful, very luxurious and modern. This review is dedicated to the staff, they are incredible and couldn’t do enough for you - Customer Service here is 10/10. A special shout out goes to Fatma at the Lobby Bar who was always smiling, attentive and always went the extra mile. Alongside her in the Lobby bar Beyza and Berkay were always welcoming, smiling and on hand making amazing drinks. The Lobby bar team speak very good english and are happy to help with any requests you may have. In the evening Mert would be making fabulous drinks in the Lobby Bar, he always remembered my order and was so professional. Lastly, Nihal from Guest Relations worked very hard to make this holiday special for me & my family as we had some some unpleasant experiences, Nihal was on hand to resolve the issue very quickly, she is a credit to this hotel.

There are many things with this hotel that require improvement such as the beach transfer vehicle and the frequency as well as cleanliness of the rooms/house keeping. Despite this, the staff and the team are a credit to this hotel as they really do work so hard and really try to make the experience of each guest memorable.', 4, 'Jul 11', null),
  ('55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555502', 'https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g1069655-d33144231-r1067634921-Azura_World_Hotel-Turkler_Alanya_Turkish_Mediterranean_Coast.html', 'New and affordable hotel. Aquapark and entertainment for small children and the elderly available. I recommend it.', 4, 'Jul 9', null)
